cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the RAPIDO 2021 paper below, which it
  reimplements.
title: "GANNoC: reward-guided GAN generation of network-on-chip topologies"
abstract: >-
  A clean-room reimplementation of the GANNoC framework: a Wasserstein GAN with
  gradient penalty whose generator is steered by a frozen reward network, used
  to generate valid network-on-chip topologies as adjacency matrices.
type: software
authors:
